feat on issue/832-mod-vise-dual-refit · PR #1027 · pinned by mod_vise_edit (a_figure_edit_regenerates_the_block_where_it_stands_in_one_undo, a_figure_edit_is_refused_by_name_and_a_lifted_jaw_warns, a_refit_after_the_stock_changed_re_picks_the_hole_and_slide_in_one_undo, a_refit_that_cannot_fit_is_refused_by_name_and_nothing_moves, a_plate_edit_that_brings_a_jaw_into_a_stock_it_was_beside_is_refused, an_edited_and_re_fitted_pair_survives_a_save), mcp_mod_vise::a_placed_pair_is_edited_and_re_fitted_over_mcp, mcp_plate (warning field), ui fixture_modvise_tests (edit, re-fit, refused re-fit) · merges at the next cut

PR #1027 covers parts 2-4 and uses `Refs #832`, so this issue stays open:
- `SetModJaw` and `RefitModVise`, each one undo step;
- the #833 review hardening;
- the MCP tools `set_mod_jaw` and `refit_mod_vise`;
- the UI row on each jaw block;
- save/load through the existing `mod_jaw` and `on_plate` keys, with no new key.

**What's left: part 1, the dual-station block. It is held back on a design question.** A setup holds one stock, and fixtures are judged per setup (`fixture::tagged`). There are two ways to give the second station its own stock, and both are unsafe:
- Take it from a second setup. That setup's program would never see the vise steel, so a gouge would go unflagged.
- Put a copy of the steel in each setup. The two copies would clash with each other.

Leaving the second station empty is not "fitted per station". The block geometry itself is simple: a second insert on the rear face, one `#[serde(default)]` field on `JawParams`. What has to come first is a multi-stock model: either several stocks in one setup, or fixtures shared across setups. That is `effort:max` or `needs-research` work, so I suggest the maintainer re-weights the remainder (I have not changed the labels). Details are in `docs/decisions/832-mod-vise-edit-refit.md` on the branch.
